<!-- Example usage of UpDownLogScaleOperator -->
<!-- This operator jointly scales parameters in log space and real space -->
<!-- Use this to maintain relationships between prevalence (log space) and scaling factors (real space) -->

<!-- EXAMPLE 1: Basic up-down operator for Deme1 -->
<!-- Prevalence (already in log space) goes UP, case counts scaling (real space) goes DOWN -->
<operator id="UpDownPrevScaling.Deme1:SimDataset"
          spec="mascotdatastreams.operators.UpDownLogScaleOperator"
          scaleFactor="0.5"
          weight="1.0">
  <!-- Prevalence parameter is ALREADY IN LOG SPACE (SkylinePrev = log(infected)) -->
  <upLogParameter idref="SkylinePrev.Deme1.t:SimDataset"/>
  <!-- Case counts scaling is IN REAL SPACE (positive real number) -->
  <downRealParameter idref="caseCounts.scaling.Deme1:SimDataset"/>
</operator>

<!-- EXAMPLE 2: Up-down operator for Deme2 -->
<operator id="UpDownPrevScaling.Deme2:SimDataset"
          spec="mascotdatastreams.operators.UpDownLogScaleOperator"
          scaleFactor="0.5"
          weight="1.0">
  <upLogParameter idref="SkylinePrev.Deme2.t:SimDataset"/>
  <downRealParameter idref="caseCounts.scaling.Deme2:SimDataset"/>
</operator>

<!-- EXAMPLE 3: Joint operator for both demes at once -->
<!-- Both demes' prevalence go up together, both scaling factors go down together -->
<operator id="UpDownPrevScaling.BothDemes:SimDataset"
          spec="mascotdatastreams.operators.UpDownLogScaleOperator"
          scaleFactor="0.3"
          weight="2.0"
          optimise="true">
  <!-- Both prevalence parameters (in log space) go up -->
  <upLogParameter idref="SkylinePrev.Deme1.t:SimDataset"/>
  <upLogParameter idref="SkylinePrev.Deme2.t:SimDataset"/>
  <!-- Both scaling parameters (in real space) go down -->
  <downRealParameter idref="caseCounts.scaling.Deme1:SimDataset"/>
  <downRealParameter idref="caseCounts.scaling.Deme2:SimDataset"/>
</operator>

<!-- EXAMPLE 4: Reverse direction - scaling up, prevalence down -->
<operator id="UpDownScalingPrev.Deme1:SimDataset"
          spec="mascotdatastreams.operators.UpDownLogScaleOperator"
          scaleFactor="0.5"
          weight="1.0">
  <!-- Scaling goes UP -->
  <upRealParameter idref="caseCounts.scaling.Deme1:SimDataset"/>
  <!-- Prevalence goes DOWN -->
  <downLogParameter idref="SkylinePrev.Deme1.t:SimDataset"/>
</operator>

<!--
HOW IT WORKS:
=============

The operator generates a single random walk step: logScaler ~ Normal(0, scaleFactor²)

For LOG-SPACE parameters (upLogParameter/downLogParameter):
  - upLogParameter:   newValue = oldValue + logScaler
  - downLogParameter: newValue = oldValue - logScaler

For REAL-SPACE parameters (upRealParameter/downRealParameter):
  - upRealParameter:   newValue = oldValue × exp(logScaler)
  - downRealParameter: newValue = oldValue × exp(-logScaler)

The Hastings ratio is automatically calculated to account for the transformations.

PARAMETER SPACE GUIDE:
======================
LOG SPACE (use upLogParameter/downLogParameter):
  - SkylinePrev.Deme*.t:SimDataset (log prevalence)
  - Any parameter stored as log(x)

REAL SPACE (use upRealParameter/downRealParameter):
  - caseCounts.scaling.Deme*:SimDataset (positive scaling factor)
  - migrationRates (positive rates)
  - Ne values (positive population sizes)

TUNING:
=======
- scaleFactor: Controls step size (typical values: 0.1-1.0)
  - Smaller = smaller steps, higher acceptance rate
  - Larger = larger steps, lower acceptance rate
- weight: Relative frequency (higher = called more often)
- optimise="true": Auto-tunes scaleFactor for ~23.4% acceptance

REPLACEMENT STRATEGY:
=====================
If you currently have separate operators like:
  <operator id="SkylinePrev.Deme1.ScalerX.t:SimDataset"
            spec="operator.kernel.BactrianRandomWalkOperator"
            parameter="@SkylinePrev.Deme1.t:SimDataset"
            scaleFactor="0.5" weight="1.0"/>
  <operator id="SkylinePrev.Deme1.ScalerXX.t:SimDataset"
            spec="kernel.BactrianScaleOperator"
            parameter="@caseCounts.scaling.Deme1:SimDataset"
            scaleFactor="0.5" weight="0.5"/>

Replace with ONE joint operator:
  <operator id="UpDownPrevScaling.Deme1:SimDataset"
            spec="mascotdatastreams.operators.UpDownLogScaleOperator"
            scaleFactor="0.5" weight="1.5">
    <upLogParameter idref="SkylinePrev.Deme1.t:SimDataset"/>
    <downRealParameter idref="caseCounts.scaling.Deme1:SimDataset"/>
  </operator>

This maintains the biological relationship: when true prevalence increases,
the case count scaling factor (detection rate) should decrease to explain
the same observed case counts.
-->
